","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer","id":8736612,"login":"kurtstohrer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MzY2MTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/5b0e798f8de2db78b6a2655a6c6568fa559c2db7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T04:05:28Z","email":"kurtstohrer@gmail.com","name":"Kurt Stohrer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T04:05:28Z","email":"kurtstohrer@gmail.com","name":"Kurt Stohrer"},"message":"fix(server): validate wireframe_apply task context at the create boundary\n\nPOST /tasks and annotask_create_task accepted an untyped `context` blob for\nevery task type, so a same-origin caller could mint a wireframe_apply task\nwhose malformed context the embedded apply agent then trusts. Add a structural\nguard — wireframe?: { route, instances[] }, session?: { session_id, entries[] }\n— on CreateTaskBody and McpCreateTaskArgs. It validates without sanitizing\n(unknown extra keys pass through; the agent only reads known fields) and only\nfires for wireframe_apply, so the live-mount \"Build this route\" payload and\nevery other task type are unaffected. Server-minted applies bypass this\nboundary entirely (applyDesignSession calls addTask directly).","tree":{"sha":"9f2c283c57b122e82aed6737dba0389b4a5d0c4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/git/trees/9f2c283c57b122e82aed6737dba0389b4a5d0c4b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/git/commits/5b0e798f8de2db78b6a2655a6c6568fa559c2db7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8736612?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer","id":8736612,"login":"kurtstohrer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MzY2MTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer/annotask/commit/5b0e798f8de2db78b6a2655a6c6568fa559c2db7","node_id":"C_kwDORzheQtoAKDViMGU3OThmOGRlMmRiNzhiNmEyNjU1YTZjNjU2OGZhNTU5YzJkYjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer/annotask/commit/9b97593cc56baa33fb94e20ec5d681f4d0c7a50e","sha":"9b97593cc56baa33fb94e20ec5d681f4d0c7a50e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/9b97593cc56baa33fb94e20ec5d681f4d0c7a50e"}],"sha":"5b0e798f8de2db78b6a2655a6c6568fa559c2db7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/5b0e798f8de2db78b6a2655a6c6568fa559c2db7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8736612?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer","id":8736612,"login":"kurtstohrer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MzY2MTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/9b97593cc56baa33fb94e20ec5d681f4d0c7a50e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T04:05:19Z","email":"kurtstohrer@gmail.com","name":"Kurt Stohrer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T04:05:19Z","email":"kurtstohrer@gmail.com","name":"Kurt Stohrer"},"message":"fix(wireframe): P0/P1 critical-review fixes + stale-viewport + composite-taint\n\nA1 generator race: cancel() bumps every supersession token, runGenerate\nre-checks ''building'' after the preview await, and updatePaletteBlock guards\n''building'' — a late in-flight preview can no longer mutate a locked sketch.\nA2: fingerprint auto-resolve honors the resolver ''capped'' flag — a sole\ncandidate needs >=0.5 under a truncated scan, so a coincidence on a monorepo\nisn''t trusted for codegen. A3: raise the upload-route body cap (6MB) so the\ndecoded 4MB PNG check is the real boundary instead of ~2.9MB. A4:\nuseWireframeDoc.load() keeps the last-good doc on a failed RE-load. A7: explode\nclaims the capture lock before its first await, falls back to rect identity for\nre-minted eids, and guards ''building''. D1: the apply batch is snapshotted\nbefore the task is minted (taskId adopted via setBatchTask; task-creation\nfailure seals the batch failed).\n\nComposite-taint: allowTaint:false at every html2canvas call site so a non-CORS\nimage rasterizes blank instead of throwing away the whole screenshot/composite,\nplus an extImages fidelity stamp + ''external images'' pill so a blank region is\na labeled cause, not a silent hole.\n\nStale-viewport: a dismissible width-mismatch banner when enter() reuses a\ncanvas captured at a different viewport, and content-weighted horizontal\ncentering of the canvas so wide captures aren''t stuck scrolled left.","tree":{"sha":"eb1c00d867951b66a8bc607863cea6392adecde8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/git/trees/eb1c00d867951b66a8bc607863cea6392adecde8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/git/commits/9b97593cc56baa33fb94e20ec5d681f4d0c7a50e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8736612?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer","id":8736612,"login":"kurtstohrer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MzY2MTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer/annotask/commit/9b97593cc56baa33fb94e20ec5d681f4d0c7a50e","node_id":"C_kwDORzheQtoAKDliOTc1OTNjYzU2YmFhMzNmYjk0ZTIwZWM1ZDY4MWY0ZDBjN2E1MGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer/annotask/commit/074deefeb9dc54f245ebe12003b99ff0a363eb6d","sha":"074deefeb9dc54f245ebe12003b99ff0a363eb6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/074deefeb9dc54f245ebe12003b99ff0a363eb6d"}],"sha":"9b97593cc56baa33fb94e20ec5d681f4d0c7a50e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/9b97593cc56baa33fb94e20ec5d681f4d0c7a50e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8736612?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer","id":8736612,"login":"kurtstohrer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MzY2MTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/074deefeb9dc54f245ebe12003b99ff0a363eb6d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T21:42:33Z","email":"kurtstohrer@gmail.com","name":"Kurt Stohrer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T21:42:33Z","email":"kurtstohrer@gmail.com","name":"Kurt Stohrer"},"message":"fix(detection,wireframe): component/data-detection defects + data-binding gate groundwork\n\nTwo coherent bodies of work on the component/data-source detection subsystem\nand the wireframe data-binding gate. The binding gate stays OFF this release\n(WIREFRAME_DATA_BINDING_ENABLED=false) — this lands the honesty groundwork only.\n\nDetection fixes (~50 P0–P3 from todo/review-component-and-data-detection-FINDINGS.md):\n- P0-1 lucide/flat-barrel OOM: exactMatchOnly barrel fallback, per-.d.ts memo,\n  size/export budget bail, worker-death no longer re-runs on main thread\n- P0-2 extraction provenance on ScannedComponent (cem|dts|dts-guessed|source|\n  name-only); MCP/ComponentsPage surface \"props unknown\" instead of implying 0\n- P0-3 workspace path-frame: resolveProjectFile retries against workspaceRoot —\n  unblocks details/shape/binding-classify/source-excerpt in monorepos\n- P0-4 data-context provenance + dep-gated identifier kinds; P0-5 project\n  components on MCP/CLI + live used_only; P0-6 standalone/webpack real bound port\n- P1/P2/P3: prop-extraction matrix, data-scanner regex + provenance\n  (endpoint_source/query_key/method_known), api-schema tRPC/Swagger2/$ref/GraphQL\n  + method/origin scoring, runtime-endpoint reconciliation, ?refresh/ETag, docs\n\nData-binding gate groundwork (flag stays off; \"groundwork, don''t flip\"):\n- WireframeDataBinding + validator gain verifiable evidence: path_source,\n  match_confidence, schema_location, schema_kind, op{method,path}, method,\n  resolved_endpoint, details_confidence; DataSourceShape carries the api-schema\n  evidence; threaded picker -> buildBinding -> wireframe directions\n- data-source-shape rung-1 admission floor (match >=0.5); real method/line\n  disambiguation (args types now accept them; api.ts casts removed); ambiguous\n  candidates carry method; DataShapeNode.variant_of marks collapsed unions\n- DataBindingPicker: ambiguity chooser (no longer coerced to blind ''none''),\n  api-schema tier requires a picked path, free-text labeled unverified assertion,\n  \"1 of N variants\" marker\n- annotask_get_data_source_shape MCP tool + `annotask data-source-shape` CLI +\n  CLAUDE.md/WIREFRAME_APPLY.md\n- gated-state hygiene: persisted bindings stripped from NEW wireframe directions\n  while gated, so \"new tasks won''t carry bindings\" is literally true\n\ntypecheck clean; 1225 tests pass (+8 new); build green.","tree":{"sha":"e84b12a433dd839ed478f70a22aa868d1e17f324","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/git/trees/e84b12a433dd839ed478f70a22aa868d1e17f324"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/git/commits/074deefeb9dc54f245ebe12003b99ff0a363eb6d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8736612?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer","id":8736612,"login":"kurtstohrer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MzY2MTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer/annotask/commit/074deefeb9dc54f245ebe12003b99ff0a363eb6d","node_id":"C_kwDORzheQtoAKDA3NGRlZWZlYjlkYzU0ZjI0NWViZTEyMDAzYjk5ZmYwYTM2M2ViNmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer/annotask/commit/afb18a63e2db5ee205d03572a3f29253d609c7ff","sha":"afb18a63e2db5ee205d03572a3f29253d609c7ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/afb18a63e2db5ee205d03572a3f29253d609c7ff"}],"sha":"074deefeb9dc54f245ebe12003b99ff0a363eb6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/074deefeb9dc54f245ebe12003b99ff0a363eb6d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8736612?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer","id":8736612,"login":"kurtstohrer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MzY2MTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/afb18a63e2db5ee205d03572a3f29253d609c7ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T00:32:23Z","email":"kurtstohrer@gmail.com","name":"Kurt Stohrer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T00:32:23Z","email":"kurtstohrer@gmail.com","name":"Kurt Stohrer"},"message":"feat(wireframe): render-once capture, capture-time fingerprint auto-resolve, fragment provenance in tasks\n\nRender-once capture: the main wireframe capture now renders the document\nONCE into a master canvas and crops every block from it — up to 25\nsequential full-document html2canvas renders become 1 (2 when an inner\nscroller exists: a plain master plus an expanded one, cropped by the same\ncontainment rule as before). The full-page ''before'' is the master\ndownscaled to scale 1, eliminating its separate render too. The master uses\nallowTaint:false deliberately — a tainted master would fail EVERY crop, so\nnon-CORS images render blank instead of poisoning the capture (the legacy\npath lost those whole blocks anyway). Oversized documents (>16384px a\nside), master failures, and crop throws all fall back silently to the\nintact legacy per-block loop; explode/refine and metaOnly probes are\nuntouched. Live-verified: instrumented vue-vite app and a proxied foreign\nsite both capture in ~530ms.\n\nCapture-time fingerprint auto-resolve: anchorless blocks now resolve\nthemselves — after capture (and explode), each block''s DOM fingerprint is\nturned into grep evidence (classes parsed from htmlHead''s first tag, since\nwalker selectors are nth-of-type-only) and run through\n/api/resolve-fingerprint; a confidently-unambiguous winner stamps\nanchor.file/line with resolvedBy:''grep''. Confidence: a sole candidate at\n>=0.3 (uniqueness across the tree IS the signal — the server''s ambiguity\ndivisor crushes boilerplate into many low candidates, and the walker''s\nconcatenated textHead rarely matches a source LINE, degrading real\nunambiguous hits to class-tier scores) or a contested leader at >=0.5 with\na 1.5x lead. Ambiguous stays honestly anchorless. The canvas chip shows\n''(grep)'' with a verify-before-trusting title; directions on grep-resolved\nanchors still carry the fingerprint plus an explicit verification note, and\nexplode/hover keep the geometric path for them (the file came from a repo\ngrep, not a DOM stamp). Live-verified end-to-end: all three blocks of a\nnever-instrumented proxied site auto-anchored to index.html:4/:6/:7.\n\nFragment provenance: getSourceData''s fragmentUrl (''POST /search'', stamped\non htmx/Turbo-swapped subtrees) now crosses the bridge boundary (four\npayload emitters) and lands everywhere it matters — wireframe block anchors\nand direction descriptions (''markup produced by POST /search; edit the\nserver template behind that endpoint''), the canvas chip for anchorless\nfragment blocks, annotation tasks (context.fragment_url on pin/arrow/\nhighlight/select/note/quick-action/general flows when the element has no\nfile), buildTaskSummary for MCP/CLI triage, and a fragment chip in the task\ndetail Source section. Fragment roots also stop the walker''s bounded anchor\nwalk, so a fragment child can never anchor up to the file whose contents\nthe swap replaced.\n\nAlso: proxy mode no longer injects the bridge into HEAD responses, and the\nplaybook''s anchorless-directions section covers grep-resolved anchors and\nfragment-produced markup (all four copies byte-synced).","tree":{"sha":"f5d14d16ec4c0468483abd5120c44e38511dd51f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/git/trees/f5d14d16ec4c0468483abd5120c44e38511dd51f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/git/commits/afb18a63e2db5ee205d03572a3f29253d609c7ff","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8736612?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer","id":8736612,"login":"kurtstohrer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MzY2MTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer/annotask/commit/afb18a63e2db5ee205d03572a3f29253d609c7ff","node_id":"C_kwDORzheQtoAKGFmYjE4YTYzZTJkYjVlZTIwNWQwMzU3MmEzZjI5MjUzZDYwOWM3ZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer/annotask/commit/52a8169be561bbfca9b3ba8e1c98e8d7bdb0810b","sha":"52a8169be561bbfca9b3ba8e1c98e8d7bdb0810b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/52a8169be561bbfca9b3ba8e1c98e8d7bdb0810b"}],"sha":"afb18a63e2db5ee205d03572a3f29253d609c7ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/afb18a63e2db5ee205d03572a3f29253d609c7ff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8736612?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer","id":8736612,"login":"kurtstohrer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MzY2MTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/52a8169be561bbfca9b3ba8e1c98e8d7bdb0810b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T23:48:08Z","email":"kurtstohrer@gmail.com","name":"Kurt Stohrer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T23:48:08Z","email":"kurtstohrer@gmail.com","name":"Kurt Stohrer"},"message":"feat(wireframe,serve): universal-site support — proxy mode, DOM fingerprints, fingerprint resolver, native debug anchors\n\nThe generality stack: capture ANY site, keep the sketch actionable, land\nanchored edits — each layer works alone and they compose.\n\nannotask serve --target <url> (universal proxy mode): hosts the full\nAnnotask server on its own port and reverse-proxies everything else to the\ntarget, injecting the bridge into proxied HTML (decompressing when needed,\nCSP/XFO stripped, redirects rewritten onto the proxy, WebSocket upgrades\ntunneled raw so HMR survives, HTML buffering bounded at 64MB). Gives\nproduction builds, CDN pages, Rails/Django/PHP, and remote staging the\ndesign tool with ZERO build integration. Verified live end-to-end with\nPlaywright against a static site that has never seen annotask.\n\nInjection corruption fix (all three injectors): the bridge was spliced in\nvia String.replace(''</body>'', script + ''</body>''), which expands $'' /\n$& REPLACEMENT PATTERNS inside the script source — the new React fiber\nkey prefix (''__reactFiber$'') expanded $'' into ''everything after the\nmatch'', truncating the script mid-token. Function replacers everywhere\n(vite SSR sniff, webpack beforeEmit, proxy).\n\nAnchorless DOM fingerprints: blocks with no source anchor now carry\n{ selector, textHead, htmlHead } from capture through the wireframe doc\ninto wireframe_apply directions, with the playbook procedure to match.\nAnchored blocks carry nothing — zero happy-path growth.\n\nresolve-fingerprint (HTTP + MCP tool + CLI): DOM evidence (class names,\ntext literal, tag) greps workspace source and returns ranked candidates —\nuniqueness-weighted so ''revenue-panel'' + ''Quarterly Revenue'' pins the exact\nfile:line while boilerplate like ''btn'' scores near zero. Closes the loop:\ncapture anywhere → fingerprint → resolve → anchored apply.\n\nNative debug-metadata anchors (bridge resolver chain): after our stamps and\nAstro''s, Svelte dev builds anchor via __svelte_meta.loc and React <=18 dev\nbuilds via fiber._debugSource (absolute fileNames cut at the last /src/;\nReact 19 degrades to component-name-only, never a fabricated file). htmx /\nTurbo swaps stamp their subtree root with ''METHOD /path'' so getSourceData\nreports ''markup produced by POST /search'' instead of mis-anchoring to an\ninstrumented ancestor.\n\nApply-session extras: undo-coverage honesty (full / anchors-only / none\ncomputed pre-mint, stamped into the task context and shown in the panel —\nan all-anchorless apply in a non-git project no longer pretends undo\nworks), cross-MFE added.module rewrite to a host-resolvable specifier, and\ndiagonal-hatch + badge on embedded-iframe canvas blocks.\n\nPlus: Nuxt/middleware-mode Vite now refuses loudly with the proxy-mode\nalternative instead of printing a success banner over a half-dead tool, and\nboot warns when a sibling MFE package is registered to a different annotask\nserver (split task stores).","tree":{"sha":"5a42672449fccaf6b1cb63c0d5b18509fff10987","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/git/trees/5a42672449fccaf6b1cb63c0d5b18509fff10987"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/git/commits/52a8169be561bbfca9b3ba8e1c98e8d7bdb0810b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8736612?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer","id":8736612,"login":"kurtstohrer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MzY2MTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer/annotask/commit/52a8169be561bbfca9b3ba8e1c98e8d7bdb0810b","node_id":"C_kwDORzheQtoAKDUyYTgxNjliZTU2MWJiZmNhOWIzYmE4ZTFjOThlOGQ3YmRiMDgxMGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer/annotask/commit/8de17a775eec11a143bbc22df8cfdf543247f52e","sha":"8de17a775eec11a143bbc22df8cfdf543247f52e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/8de17a775eec11a143bbc22df8cfdf543247f52e"}],"sha":"52a8169be561bbfca9b3ba8e1c98e8d7bdb0810b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/52a8169be561bbfca9b3ba8e1c98e8d7bdb0810b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8736612?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer","id":8736612,"login":"kurtstohrer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MzY2MTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/8de17a775eec11a143bbc22df8cfdf543247f52e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T21:45:35Z","email":"kurtstohrer@gmail.com","name":"Kurt Stohrer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T21:45:35Z","email":"kurtstohrer@gmail.com","name":"Kurt Stohrer"},"message":"feat(wireframe): shadow-DOM descent and iframe-boundary honesty in the walker\n\nWeb-component apps (Lit/Shoelace-style, all content in an open shadow root)\nused to collapse to ONE undecomposable block: discovery only walked light\nDOM, even though html2canvas-pro renders open shadow content fine. The\nwalker now descends open shadow roots when an element has no qualifying\nlight children — slots resolve to their assigned elements (fallback content\nat the slot position) — and the geometric re-resolver sweeps shadow trees\nafter the light scan. Closed shadow hosts can''t be descended; they stamp\nmeta.fidelity ''shadow-opaque'' so the limitation is explicit, not silent.\n\n<iframe> is now an explicit opaque leaf: it still emits a block (its\ngeometry and host anchor are real — moving the mount is legitimate) but is\nstamped embedded:''iframe'', is never descended, and explode refuses it with\n''annotate it from its own dev server'' instead of decomposing blank\ncross-origin pixels into nonsense. The flag persists onto the wireframe\nblock so the guard survives reloads.\n\nLight-DOM pages produce a byte-identical block set (regression-pinned).","tree":{"sha":"ef3d3595d6960b0feee28642b57daf6192360aa5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/git/trees/ef3d3595d6960b0feee28642b57daf6192360aa5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/git/commits/8de17a775eec11a143bbc22df8cfdf543247f52e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8736612?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer","id":8736612,"login":"kurtstohrer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MzY2MTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer/annotask/commit/8de17a775eec11a143bbc22df8cfdf543247f52e","node_id":"C_kwDORzheQtoAKDhkZTE3YTc3NWVlYzExYTE0M2JiYzIyZGY4Y2ZkZjU0MzI0N2Y1MmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer/annotask/commit/1c071a0f14b68dae54616a42aed02f4c888fc3d3","sha":"1c071a0f14b68dae54616a42aed02f4c888fc3d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/1c071a0f14b68dae54616a42aed02f4c888fc3d3"}],"sha":"8de17a775eec11a143bbc22df8cfdf543247f52e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/8de17a775eec11a143bbc22df8cfdf543247f52e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8736612?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer","id":8736612,"login":"kurtstohrer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MzY2MTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/1c071a0f14b68dae54616a42aed02f4c888fc3d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T21:29:31Z","email":"kurtstohrer@gmail.com","name":"Kurt Stohrer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T21:29:31Z","email":"kurtstohrer@gmail.com","name":"Kurt Stohrer"},"message":"fix(wireframe): capture robustness — lazy-content warm-up, inner-scroller normalization, per-render deadlines\n\nThree verified failure classes on real-world pages, all in the bridge\ncapture handler (messages.ts):\n\n- Lazy content captured blank: capture jumped straight to scrollTo(0,0), so\n  IntersectionObserver-driven loaders and reveal-on-scroll content below the\n  fold never fired. Full captures now sweep the window AND the primary inner\n  scroller through the page in viewport-sized steps (bounded ~25 steps),\n  wait for document.fonts.ready (bounded 1.5s), and settle before\n  discovery. The metaOnly hover probe never scrolls and explode re-captures\n  already-loaded content — both skip the sweep (payload.skipWarmup is the\n  escape hatch).\n\n- Inner-scroll-container layouts (the standard dashboard shell: html/body\n  overflow:hidden, one big element scrolls) got zero normalization — the\n  scroller''s offset skewed every rect and its clip hid below-fold content.\n  The primary scroller (largest scrollable) is now reset to origin for the\n  capture and restored after; blocks INSIDE it crop from an html2canvas\n  clone with the scroller un-clipped (their live rects already ignore\n  clipping, so geometry matches), while blocks after it in flow keep the\n  unexpanded clone so their crops don''t shift. Reported docHeight includes\n  the scroller''s hidden extent.\n\n- One slow render discarded everything: the shell''s 60s whole-capture\n  timeout was the only guard over up to 25 sequential full-document\n  renders, each willing to wait html2canvas''s default 15s per image. Every\n  render now has its own deadline (12s block/shell, 20s full page) that\n  degrades to that block''s meta.error, and imageTimeout is capped at 3s.\n\nVerified end-to-end: emitted-bridge parse check plus a live Playwright probe\nagainst the vue-vite playground (wireframe mode → 4 captured blocks with\nreal pixels through the new warm-up → normalize → render pipeline).","tree":{"sha":"e6a93db301e101b37f28b0b873f653ad18a06f8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/git/trees/e6a93db301e101b37f28b0b873f653ad18a06f8a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/git/commits/1c071a0f14b68dae54616a42aed02f4c888fc3d3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8736612?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer","id":8736612,"login":"kurtstohrer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MzY2MTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer/annotask/commit/1c071a0f14b68dae54616a42aed02f4c888fc3d3","node_id":"C_kwDORzheQtoAKDFjMDcxYTBmMTRiNjhkYWU1NDYxNmE0MmFlZDAyZjRjODg4ZmMzZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer/annotask/commit/3b738ae5e642558f5a9646a53b343ae4f36cd28a","sha":"3b738ae5e642558f5a9646a53b343ae4f36cd28a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/3b738ae5e642558f5a9646a53b343ae4f36cd28a"}],"sha":"1c071a0f14b68dae54616a42aed02f4c888fc3d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/1c071a0f14b68dae54616a42aed02f4c888fc3d3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8736612?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer","id":8736612,"login":"kurtstohrer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MzY2MTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/3b738ae5e642558f5a9646a53b343ae4f36cd28a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T21:19:58Z","email":"kurtstohrer@gmail.com","name":"Kurt Stohrer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T21:19:58Z","email":"kurtstohrer@gmail.com","name":"Kurt Stohrer"},"message":"fix(wireframe): loop-anchor safety, exploded-move dedup, monorepo undo coverage, MFE anchor attribution\n\nDirections (sketch → source contract):\n- Blocks sharing one (file,line) anchor (v-for/map loop items) now carry\n  sharedAnchor {ordinal, of} and an explicit caution — a delete on one loop\n  card no longer reads as ''delete the loop''; the agent is told a source-level\n  edit hits every instance and to verify via binding classification.\n- Dragging an exploded parent no longer emits N+1 independent move\n  directions: children whose delta matches the parent''s (±2px) are\n  suppressed (''its children move with it''); children that genuinely moved\n  within the container say so.\n- Moves whose overlap-gated relations come back empty get a nearest-block\n  fallback relation (pixels-only directions violated the playbook''s own\n  ''intent over pixels'' contract); adds name a runner-up anchor donor when\n  the choice was a close call.\n- Note directions carry their block''s rect so badge numbering stays\n  spatially top-down instead of pinning notes to y=0.\n\nWalker: the chrome pass now applies the same 48x24 footprint as the other\npasses plus off-document (<25% overlap) and opacity:0 filters — skip-nav at\nleft:-9999px stops minting blank blocks that eat the 24-block cap. Rejected\nchrome stays in the containment set so it can''t resurface as a straggler.\n\nSnapshot engine (the byte-exact undo guarantee):\n- Monorepo baselines: the git machinery now runs at the repo toplevel when\n  it is an ancestor of projectRoot inside the workspace root, translating\n  repo-relative paths to projectRoot-relative (''../mfe-x/…'') both ways —\n  the auto-extend and created-file nets were silently OFF in exactly the\n  pnpm/yarn workspace topology multi-MFE uses. Toplevel persists per batch\n  so rehydrated batches seal correctly.\n- Staged new files: a file the agent created AND ''git add''-ed (''A '', not\n  ''??'') is now hashed into the created net at seal — undo/discard no longer\n  silently leave it behind.\n\nMFE anchor attribution (server-side wrong-file guard): applyDesignSession\nverifies every anchor claiming an MFE actually resolves under that MFE''s\npackage dir — re-rooting package-local paths when the file exists there,\nrefusing the apply otherwise — before the dominant file, task context, and\nsnapshot set read it. Closes the silent path where a capture racing the\nclient-side workspace-catalog load persisted src/App.vue and the agent then\nedited (and undo ''correctly'' restored) the HOST''s same-named file. The\ncatalog now also sniffs webpack configs for AnnotaskWebpackPlugin mfe ids,\nand the shell awaits the catalog before building anchors at capture time.\n\nDocs: WIREFRAME_APPLY.md (+ mirrors) and CLAUDE.md corrected — explode is\nON this release (MFE-aware, geometric fallback); only data binding is gated\noff. Delete-op rule gains the loop-anchor caveat.","tree":{"sha":"b86a961dc4cdf7d96f25571eefebdaae8ea39e4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/git/trees/b86a961dc4cdf7d96f25571eefebdaae8ea39e4b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/git/commits/3b738ae5e642558f5a9646a53b343ae4f36cd28a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8736612?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer","id":8736612,"login":"kurtstohrer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MzY2MTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer/annotask/commit/3b738ae5e642558f5a9646a53b343ae4f36cd28a","node_id":"C_kwDORzheQtoAKDNiNzM4YWU1ZTY0MjU1OGY1YTk2NDZhNTNiMzQzYWU0ZjM2Y2QyOGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer/annotask/commit/40e851c2fef2ccc4ea32446680be91f14b1d0a60","sha":"40e851c2fef2ccc4ea32446680be91f14b1d0a60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/40e851c2fef2ccc4ea32446680be91f14b1d0a60"}],"sha":"3b738ae5e642558f5a9646a53b343ae4f36cd28a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/3b738ae5e642558f5a9646a53b343ae4f36cd28a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8736612?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer","id":8736612,"login":"kurtstohrer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MzY2MTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/40e851c2fef2ccc4ea32446680be91f14b1d0a60/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T21:02:08Z","email":"kurtstohrer@gmail.com","name":"Kurt Stohrer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T21:02:08Z","email":"kurtstohrer@gmail.com","name":"Kurt Stohrer"},"message":"feat(agent): even out the four local CLIs — session resume, capability probes, batch chaining, MCP wiring\n\nSession resume (all 4 CLIs): providers parse their CLI''s session envelope\ninto a shared ''session'' event, persist it on the turn''s thread message, and\nfollow-up turns spawn the CLI''s native resume (claude --resume, codex exec\nresume, opencode --session, copilot --resume) with ONLY the delta message —\nno more replaying the system prompt + full transcript into every cold spawn.\nA resume attempt that dies contentless (stale session) is discarded wholesale\nvia a pre-content holdback and silently retried cold, so no turn is ever\nlost (verified against claude''s real stale shape, which echoes the bogus id\nback in an error result envelope).\n\nCapability probes: agent-detect greps each CLI''s help text (one spawn, many\npatterns) for resume / --append-system-prompt (claude) / stdin prompt\n(codex); the runner forwards flags via StreamOptions.cliCapabilities so an\nold CLI never receives a flag it can''t parse.\n\nToken efficiency: claude cold spawns ship the composed skill prompt via\n--append-system-prompt (cacheable system segment, adjacent to Claude Code''s\nown cached prefix); codex moves the prompt off argv onto stdin (''- ''\npositional; 4x history budget, nothing leaks into ps); the volatile\npermission-mode directive is appended instead of prepended so the stable\nskill prefix stays byte-identical across runs.\n\nBatch chaining: the auto-run driver keeps the CLI session left by each\nheadless run and hands it to the next queued task of the SAME type +\nresolved provider as a resume target — tasks 2..N of a ''run pending'' batch\nskip the CLI bootstrap, the 22-39KB skill prompt, and re-reading files the\nprevious task already explored. Chain-compatible tasks jump the FIFO;\nrecycles at 100K input tokens of session context; drops on any failure.\nSettings > Providers gains a ''Token efficiency'' kill switch (default on).\n\nUsage honesty: CLIs that report no (or output-only — copilot) usage now get\ncharacter-length estimates flagged estimated:true, plumbed thread -> task\nrollup -> usage.jsonl; the Usage panel notes how many turns are estimates.\n\nMCP wiring parity: annotask init-mcp gains codex (~/.codex/config.toml, TOML\nmerge preserving foreign tables), opencode (project opencode.json), and\ncopilot (~/.copilot/mcp-config.json) targets — spawned codex/opencode/\ncopilot runs finally get annotask tools without hand-editing configs.","tree":{"sha":"8eccd8f27af697c7df1bf05379bed6c2f0c91abb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/git/trees/8eccd8f27af697c7df1bf05379bed6c2f0c91abb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/git/commits/40e851c2fef2ccc4ea32446680be91f14b1d0a60","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8736612?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer","id":8736612,"login":"kurtstohrer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MzY2MTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer/annotask/commit/40e851c2fef2ccc4ea32446680be91f14b1d0a60","node_id":"C_kwDORzheQtoAKDQwZTg1MWMyZmVmMmNjYzRlYTMyNDQ2NjgwYmU5MWYxNGIxZDBhNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer/annotask/commit/e7f27a4ee1c22051feee7573c493fc2c969c09c5","sha":"e7f27a4ee1c22051feee7573c493fc2c969c09c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/e7f27a4ee1c22051feee7573c493fc2c969c09c5"}],"sha":"40e851c2fef2ccc4ea32446680be91f14b1d0a60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/40e851c2fef2ccc4ea32446680be91f14b1d0a60"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8736612?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kurtstohrer","id":8736612,"login":"kurtstohrer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MzY2MTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kurtstohrer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kurtstohrer/annotask/commits/e7f27a4ee1c22051feee7573c493fc2c969c09c5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-24T15:17:44Z","email":"kurtstohrer@gmail.com","name":"Kurt Stohrer"},"comment_count":0,"committer"