izations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bochek/bochek-mission-control/commits/065d9f408297c044a1e893b43fc4ec02a29df267/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-14T14:03:02Z","email":"93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"nyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-14T14:03:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: docker compose pids location + clear stale update banner\n\n- Move pids limit from service-level `pids_limit` to\n  `deploy.resources.limits.pids` for Compose v5+ compatibility.\n  Some Compose versions normalize both into the same field, causing\n  \"can''t set distinct values\" errors.\n\n- Clear OpenClaw update banner when `/api/openclaw/version` reports\n  `updateAvailable: false`. Previously the banner could persist after\n  a successful update because only the `true` path was handled.\n\nCloses #353, closes #351","tree":{"sha":"f25e5089324fe056686aec554b2248a5aa81d9e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bochek/bochek-mission-control/git/trees/f25e5089324fe056686aec554b2248a5aa81d9e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bochek/bochek-mission-control/git/commits/065d9f408297c044a1e893b43fc4ec02a29df267","verification":{"payload":"tree f25e5089324fe056686aec554b2248a5aa81d9e8\nparent ae39b9b1906ba5079638b3923eadd43c8f4e3c13\nauthor nyk <93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com> 1773496982 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773496982 +0700\n\nfix: docker compose pids location + clear stale update banner\n\n- Move pids limit from service-level `pids_limit` to\n  `deploy.resources.limits.pids` for Compose v5+ compatibility.\n  Some Compose versions normalize both into the same field, causing\n  \"can''t set distinct values\" errors.\n\n- Clear OpenClaw update banner when `/api/openclaw/version` reports\n  `updateAvailable: false`. Previously the banner could persist after\n  a successful update because only the `true` path was handled.\n\nCloses #353, closes #351","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJptWqWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdOgQAGCez401OctvKPB8GulYL2ZZ\nkoyx6crSANdZukmsEzxTle+zTMoan43zwnymko8p7PAtvPrHzW5R4N8+2s87Sn6s\n7qwqbbFvh0467zKh8erdoUQJFGsV5Fh493CcYStVlxtN+5hfA6OsJh+YCYXBl3Kf\nCJgF9Xux8AFiPqCqsE7h5TqPq/DlFSpOWoMUv/ICbYOMF31EcIcR7rKBLKfv3sCf\nhlbeiXuc7J2yaxuStTXaRKNzHCS0hELS4fD+V6A4VCeEZx41Hf+DC6r1mNF7Nw1f\nmEz1Tm9DolC56Dduj82EGonmd2RIn6p17JkZkPDK+b1U4YIkToqc9SzeQMFqFUGC\n8i5vBct1nyn9gwCdkPIwVxVylYC/qYiPJvkuS2M0E3FDRfvOlchw2i2NpcSBvW3h\n6SJ9Tg1hR6yR88l809iiq6eGKYjsx5MvnNKuS4xFE2L/Et7hcI0WYfSYNWWJJUfT\n5bH5O4pYhtez+ruQ8743W9HKQnfa0ERCc2sBRNqQDxM1k38xamjOPmR1F2dMbQeT\nKo89z5oLUzWYd/1+hJXaB3wyhw50rDBvz+2RaO5A9V2ZNw7KJVs+u8pBEujcRV3g\nMGctFeaQEz6OXj3ytQR71MFxnXsTKlqeqL25I4esJks2P/JiYyDhnFerzbFChcMm\nd2QHIeV9HUX7qPUZNQqE\n=G6eQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-29T06:06:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/bochek/bochek-mission-control/commit/065d9f408297c044a1e893b43fc4ec02a29df267","node_id":"C_kwDORzq8ntoAKDA2NWQ5ZjQwODI5N2MwNDRhMWU4OTNiNDNmYzRlYzAyYTI5ZGYyNjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bochek/bochek-mission-control/commit/ae39b9b1906ba5079638b3923eadd43c8f4e3c13","sha":"ae39b9b1906ba5079638b3923eadd43c8f4e3c13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bochek/bochek-mission-control/commits/ae39b9b1906ba5079638b3923eadd43c8f4e3c13"}],"sha":"065d9f408297c044a1e893b43fc4ec02a29df267","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bochek/bochek-mission-control/commits/065d9f408297c044a1e893b43fc4ec02a29df267"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/264638470?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/HonzysClawdbot","id":264638470,"login":"HonzysClawdbot","node_id":"U_kgDOD8YQBg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bochek/bochek-mission-control/commits/ae39b9b1906ba5079638b3923eadd43c8f4e3c13/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-14T13:46:32Z","email":"janclawdbotstratil@gmail.com","name":"HonzysClawdbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-14T13:46:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: add Docker-mode integration tests for gateway connectivity regressions\n\n* fix: show all agents in command select, disable those without active session\n\nPreviously the agent select in the OrchestrationBar only listed agents\nwith a session_key set (agents.filter(a => a.session_key)), causing the\ndropdown to appear completely empty when agents exist but none have an\nactive session. This was confusing — users thought no agents were\nregistered.\n\nFix: show all registered agents in the dropdown. Agents without an\nactive session_key are shown as disabled with a ''— no session'' suffix\nand a tooltip explaining why they can''t be messaged. The ''No agents\nregistered'' placeholder is shown only when the agents array is truly\nempty.\n\nThe send button remains correctly disabled when no valid agent is\nselected.\n\nFixes #321\n\n* test: add gateway health history e2e + utility unit tests\n\n- Add tests/gateway-health-history.spec.ts: Playwright e2e tests for\n  GET /api/gateways/health/history and POST /api/gateways/health\n  covering auth guards, response shape validation, chronological\n  ordering, and gateway name resolution.\n\n- Add src/app/api/gateways/health/health-utils.test.ts: 30 vitest\n  unit tests for the pure utility functions in the health probe route:\n  ipv4InCidr, isBlockedUrl (SSRF protection), buildGatewayProbeUrl,\n  parseGatewayVersion, and hasOpenClaw32ToolsProfileRisk.\n\nAll 30 unit tests pass. Covers the health history feature introduced\nin feat(gateways): add health history logging and timeline (#300).\n\n* test: add Docker-mode integration tests for gateway connectivity regressions\n\nCovers three post-fix regression scenarios:\n- 404 on gateway health (wizard used GET; endpoint is POST-only) — #334\n- EROFS / build-phase DB eager init in Docker — #337\n- Gateway connect resolves ws_url without OPENCLAW_HOME env var\n\nAdds tests/docker-mode.spec.ts with four describe blocks:\n1. Gateway health endpoint contract (POST=200, GET=405, no-auth=401)\n2. Lazy DB init on first runtime request (read + write paths)\n3. Gateway connect without home env vars\n4. Onboarding gateway-link step lifecycle","tree":{"sha":"26e707e35039290ccbba50016cda65d36c89463b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bochek/bochek-mission-control/git/trees/26e707e35039290ccbba50016cda65d36c89463b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bochek/bochek-mission-control/git/commits/ae39b9b1906ba5079638b3923eadd43c8f4e3c13","verification":{"payload":"tree 26e707e35039290ccbba50016cda65d36c89463b\nparent e2ddf09a7217e76b3143d18a4e8b1a9e693d217a\nauthor HonzysClawdbot <janclawdbotstratil@gmail.com> 1773495992 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773495992 +0700\n\ntest: add Docker-mode integration tests for gateway connectivity regressions\n\n* fix: show all agents in command select, disable those without active session\n\nPreviously the agent select in the OrchestrationBar only listed agents\nwith a session_key set (agents.filter(a => a.session_key)), causing the\ndropdown to appear completely empty when agents exist but none have an\nactive session. This was confusing — users thought no agents were\nregistered.\n\nFix: show all registered agents in the dropdown. Agents without an\nactive session_key are shown as disabled with a ''— no session'' suffix\nand a tooltip explaining why they can''t be messaged. The ''No agents\nregistered'' placeholder is shown only when the agents array is truly\nempty.\n\nThe send button remains correctly disabled when no valid agent is\nselected.\n\nFixes #321\n\n* test: add gateway health history e2e + utility unit tests\n\n- Add tests/gateway-health-history.spec.ts: Playwright e2e tests for\n  GET /api/gateways/health/history and POST /api/gateways/health\n  covering auth guards, response shape validation, chronological\n  ordering, and gateway name resolution.\n\n- Add src/app/api/gateways/health/health-utils.test.ts: 30 vitest\n  unit tests for the pure utility functions in the health probe route:\n  ipv4InCidr, isBlockedUrl (SSRF protection), buildGatewayProbeUrl,\n  parseGatewayVersion, and hasOpenClaw32ToolsProfileRisk.\n\nAll 30 unit tests pass. Covers the health history feature introduced\nin feat(gateways): add health history logging and timeline (#300).\n\n* test: add Docker-mode integration tests for gateway connectivity regressions\n\nCovers three post-fix regression scenarios:\n- 404 on gateway health (wizard used GET; endpoint is POST-only) — #334\n- EROFS / build-phase DB eager init in Docker — #337\n- Gateway connect resolves ws_url without OPENCLAW_HOME env var\n\nAdds tests/docker-mode.spec.ts with four describe blocks:\n1. Gateway health endpoint contract (POST=200, GET=405, no-auth=401)\n2. Lazy DB init on first runtime request (read + write paths)\n3. Gateway connect without home env vars\n4. Onboarding gateway-link step lifecycle","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJptWa4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMBwQABGi7nNMTdAWcZ0C5TeDv/3L\neFFnSau9HFQZuI1eBsj7mWVVorEgY9zXr44c1fABH7EZjfhsiwVKkKv+E35no1B9\nPrbUxabdp4bUiGVnj2aPkhx63s8fx7iN0EWr7h53cGjMFRZSpncDUOns50ikpqoR\nHpWFbngp4w+1xzhm71najTV2tiipixxlOoiIjBXv+/Eq9EQgKUhWGUuf3wFvbwzq\no6yKlZsekeNf+JggcM5ayvc+eluQhtMJdb/n9jPdQSLWRNL411QLdOjopcJyfjvP\nuJ06m0bEHXal64DaKgymEzjI07e29ROHqivWaal5u8RrrANq+HKAHCRZMSQJ1OKb\nlI1GhDg2r5avRbgW5PSoaDw5y/JtaJdR/G5sxZDLOx2KhldDBg5LVN9xH3VhQera\nDjlpSL66S/WzEL2LNI2ERYprrAQhkfpwrno6RHhEXkGRQiEH/tuI6/ggmr/W7rDY\nYb3wmSTN3I4mr793JKk21ku8YgHxrUUR41yurcdxsXJANBVWBBnjXBpGi24kQ7YQ\nyZKbJBc67xx0x9nE5gQ5KONE9sCR5ogvnjVbWy4D7HUpUK1EW61oRFnAY0j3yMNO\nRe7enoyjhbNDgRvipMcwLCgAwmoQxonH3b8kP3KwSFpXhAa79PMw1eBRi/WIOOD7\ndzqm9MCUopnycs7ncTyM\n=Y8Lm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE---