:"mildcodes","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0NjU3NzIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mildcodes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mildcodes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mildcodes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mildcodes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mildcodes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mildcodes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/retemper/esmap/commits/e1669a10c0d19773cc3f5fceb7534effabf64755/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-31T23:39:03Z","email":"44657722+devKangMinHyeok@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Minhyeok Kang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-31T23:39:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ssr): add @esmap/ssr package for server-side rendering (#7)\n\n* feat(ssr): add @esmap/ssr package for server-side rendering support\n\nCloses the biggest gap in esmap vs other MFE frameworks: W3C Import Maps\nare browser-only, so SSR requires a separate module resolution strategy.\n\nNew package provides:\n- Server-side import map resolver (W3C algorithm on Node.js)\n- ESM module loader with fetch + temp-file evaluation\n- SSR renderer orchestrator with ssrRender convention\n- React SSR helpers (renderReactToString, createReactSsrRender)\n- HTML document composer with import map embedding\n- Client hydration adapter (createReactHydrationApp)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(ssr): translate all test descriptions to English\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: format pnpm-lock.yaml\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9462f8d6419fd5d7204e156e1006de6044ddde7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/retemper/esmap/git/trees/9462f8d6419fd5d7204e156e1006de6044ddde7c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/retemper/esmap/git/commits/e1669a10c0d19773cc3f5fceb7534effabf64755","verification":{"payload":"tree 9462f8d6419fd5d7204e156e1006de6044ddde7c\nparent 7fb92e8af4749c2f5f0e6d7339a93e15becf649f\nauthor Minhyeok Kang <44657722+devKangMinHyeok@users.noreply.github.com> 1775000343 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1775000343 +0000\n\nfeat(ssr): add @esmap/ssr package for server-side rendering (#7)\n\n* feat(ssr): add @esmap/ssr package for server-side rendering support\n\nCloses the biggest gap in esmap vs other MFE frameworks: W3C Import Maps\nare browser-only, so SSR requires a separate module resolution strategy.\n\nNew package provides:\n- Server-side import map resolver (W3C algorithm on Node.js)\n- ESM module loader with fetch + temp-file evaluation\n- SSR renderer orchestrator with ssrRender convention\n- React SSR helpers (renderReactToString, createReactSsrRender)\n- HTML document composer with import map embedding\n- Client hydration adapter (createReactHydrationApp)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(ssr): translate all test descriptions to English\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: format pnpm-lock.yaml\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpzFsXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAA3MQAHn8JX913NMmCVz+yzKjKWQo\nz2kxnQYr9XPXEvcgBUCb/rPrccGKWBse8w1PmRsjSlFu0rfs1xgz//xsxYs0HhJP\nIe0kSUInqeTbou6gHqpyiRXUrNT9k2CYu8f8+5wdHkEQlq3Ii3U96jtZkccrsVTZ\nQaKYsSlMDpOj4sj0QVGAezGnQ6zdjqS6EUgIylVZUv8Aa8Sev2EKsCNqzy1aX8xU\nRupuOEAfj/eqvxDVeCRBCVZNl1I1+o5rK5oubBkinDv+a35dbyJfzd6+VM7kMUHw\nm9SquPnqbKPoitiZ+qo2TeU4G4cgC15KYp9cUxTGBY8N0x5NVjSURD8uWva6dfMa\nZFJyCcBm0UlAALv7SPO/eQ2AKV6UrKsHN77ZSjuqR95z93xSCXr63PR1X3agmDDa\nh2Axv1T013fg+ARdHyMPIt0Qu14Oh//mcW+QN8gR9MkHgCvwYM