587ee6a5c629f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/264638470?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/HonzysClawdbot","id":264638470,"login":"HonzysClawdbot","node_id":"U_kgDOD8YQBg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/classical91/mission-control/commits/0acf7daf320dd7b0a4e1dbbe506af7a4ad0cdeac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-16T04:34:28Z","email":"janclawdbotstratil@gmail.com","name":"HonzysClawdbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-16T04:34:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: task assignment session targeting (#399)\n\n* feat: add task session targeting - dispatch tasks to specific agent sessions (#395)\n\nWhen assigning a task to an agent, users can now optionally select an\nexisting session to dispatch the task to instead of creating a new one.\n\nChanges:\n- task-dispatch.ts: When target_session is set in task metadata, use\n  gateway chat.send to dispatch to that specific session instead of\n  creating a new one via call agent\n- task-board-panel.tsx: Add session selector dropdown in both Create\n  and Edit task modals that appears when an agent is selected and has\n  active sessions\n- store/index.ts: Add agent and channel fields to Session interface\n\nCloses #395\n\n* fix(gateway): ensure gateways table exists before health probe\n\nThe gateways table is created lazily by the gateways API (ensureTable).\nThe health route was querying it directly without CREATE IF NOT EXISTS,\ncausing SqliteError: no such table: gateways in fresh databases (E2E tests,\nDocker first-boot).\n\nAdd ensureGatewaysTable() inline to mirror the pattern in route.ts.","tree":{"sha":"4d8bc162ed0bf6a7d607b4083c538e2fac9c470b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/classical91/mission-control/git/trees/4d8bc162ed0bf6a7d607b4083c538e2fac9c470b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/classical91/mission-control/git/commits/0acf7daf320dd7b0a4e1dbbe506af7a4ad0cdeac","verification":{"payload":"tree 4d8bc162ed0bf6a7d607b4083c538e2fac9c470b\nparent e7aa7e6a917715e52b40f1d5012f1402f6a5209d\nauthor HonzysClawdbot <janclawdbotstratil@gmail.com> 1773635668 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773635668 +0700\n\nfeat: task assignment session targeting (#399)\n\n* feat: add task session targeting - dispatch tasks to specific agent sessions (#395)\n\nWhen assigning a task to an agent, users can now optionally select an\nexisting session to dispatch the task to instead of creating a new one.\n\nChanges:\n- task-dispatch.ts: When target_session is set in task metadata, use\n  gateway chat.send to dispatch to that specific session instead of\n  creating a new one via call agent\n- task-board-panel.tsx: Add session selector dropdown in both Create\n  and Edit task modals that appears when an agent is selected and has\n  active sessions\n- store/index.ts: Add agent and channel fields to Session interface\n\nCloses #395\n\n* fix(gateway): ensure gateways table exists before health probe\n\nThe gateways table is created lazily by the gateways API (ensureTable).\nThe health route was querying it directly without CREATE IF NOT EXISTS,\ncausing SqliteError: no such table: gateways in fresh databases (E2E tests,\nDocker first-boot).\n\nAdd ensureGatewaysTable() inline to mirror the pattern in route.ts.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpt4hUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbDMQAA1aWBa9hgC9K50XOOEAkRjN\n8KJL39AgUdJrf/Fmznx61SKlCH3222f3/rfGPTxYs/UGOc1b344jmqeB0+D0mSuC\n5gkP28oeviz8CVq065a/fpsMW6HPy/FqYVA4dXUjWvIICCxBhLmOE2HcyNCfUGzl\nIuZKyYHSDHcWqdvnsIILGqg7782e3wC8nSfOdaDbBJ7LUVJQr//S2hpYhjiVXotO\nxuXoQu/+SlpLXU+Ui5lpGNhaxo9GKhsgMBTZNiaUCnbpnJbu0c7vsEoQ0UV4uLui\n9hxjpBooMk4V6OB9VVTHi22yRESnAbHVFWZzayfo3rSqd05+n2DXiBNKO6ygSiFW\noX3RCoEVjYHAhvq2Vr0YDAhqVZYuKng9R0/7c5A7AuY/Zpd7Z0nHDJ/BBpT/spFH\nRTKbYQo8MbJw8n8jQYk4yBcdZVUWnpiw4wTkv09pckF/KPWJ5QVzZDVaBqHes8PX\nEbLpeOadbeFwJbxSZcZhWgPoP/RpUfSpebZ6XLyFTnjiQ8C//gQJiZkh7inWtNbk\ngCOvNZSAcPx3vW17gQ6V32Cspqd61cZ9x/+zecuwZdNjyHiC+zLj7SxVfsDdLF53\nQPabABLXkwO2J/mkwI1qAZsJNw/MATWSyOKGNPBUuvlhxIgHbDt9v0oE7/ikgpAs\nFshIvoHUmCLnqR/AbA62\n=NA/N\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-29T13:55:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/classical91/mission-control/commit/0acf7daf320dd7b0a4e1dbbe506af7a4ad0cdeac","node_id":"C_kwDORz7BONoAKDBhY2Y3ZGFmMzIwZGQ3YjBhNGUxZGJiZTUwNmFmN2E0YWQwY2RlYWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/classical91/mission-control/commit/e7aa7e6a917715e52b40f1d5012f1402f6a5209d","sha":"e7aa7e6a917715e52b40f1d5012f1402f6a5209d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/classical91/mission-control/commits/e7aa7e6a917715e52b40f1d5012f1402f6a5209d"}],"sha":"0acf7daf320dd7b0a4e1dbbe506af7a4ad0cdeac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/classical91/mission-control/commits/0acf7daf320dd7b0a4e1dbbe506af7a4ad0cdeac"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93952610?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/0xNyk","id":93952610,"login":"0xNyk","node_id":"U_kgDOBZmaYg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/classical91/mission-control/commits/e7aa7e6a917715e52b40f1d5012f1402f6a5209d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-16T04:30:02Z","email":"93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"nyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-16T04:30:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: reduce server memory footprint (#405)\n\n* fix: reduce server memory footprint across session parsing, caching, and rate limiting\n\n- Stream-parse Claude JSONL session files instead of loading entire files into memory\n- Add 50MB file size cap to skip oversized session transcripts\n- Add 30s TTL cache to getAllGatewaySessions() to avoid redundant disk reads per scheduler tick\n- Cap rate limiter maps at 10,000 entries with oldest-first eviction\n- Add request.signal abort listener to SSE route for defense-in-depth cleanup\n- Add test for rate limiter maxEntries eviction behavior\n\n* fix: address audit findings across all memory-fix files\n\nclaude-sessions.ts:\n- Wrap readline loop in try/finally to ensure rl.close() on error paths\n- Guard statSync in file loop to handle files deleted between readdir and stat\n- Fix variable shadowing: rename inner `now` to `nowSec` to avoid confusion\n- Update throttle timestamp on empty scan results (prevents repeated disk scans)\n- Skip sidechain-only sessions (zero user+assistant messages)\n\nsessions.ts:\n- Decouple `active` flag from cache — compute at read time to prevent stale data\n- Remove activeWithinMs from cache key to eliminate cache thrashing between\n  callers using different windows (Infinity vs default)\n- Add invalidateSessionCache() and call it after pruneGatewaySessionsOlderThan\n\nevents/route.ts:\n- Null out cleanup after first call to prevent double-invoke\n- Remove unnecessary `if (request.signal)` guard (always defined on NextRequest)\n\nrate-limit.test.ts:\n- Rewrite eviction test with maxRequests=1 to actually prove eviction occurred\n- Add assertion that non-evicted entries remain tracked","tree":{"sha":"539b04a949685db826fa9feea060200e45c40958","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/classical91/mission-control/git/trees/539b04a949685db826fa9feea060200e45c40958"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/classical91/mission-control/git/commits/e7aa7e6a917715e52b40f1d5012f1402f6a5209d","verification":{"payload":"tree 539b04a949685db826fa9feea060200e45c40958\nparent b6717b8bf8d21c0cb9a9b82de1478049787f49e1\nauthor nyk <93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com> 1773635402 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773635402 +0700\n\nfix: reduce server memory footprint (#405)\n\n* fix: reduce server memory footprint across session parsing, caching, and rate limiting\n\n- Stream-parse Claude JSONL session files instead of loading entire files into memory\n- Add 50MB file size cap to skip oversized session transcripts\n- Add 30s TTL cache to getAllGatewaySessions() to avoid redundant disk reads per scheduler tick\n- Cap rate limiter maps at 10,000 entries with oldest-first eviction\n- Add request.signal abort listener to SSE route for defense-in-depth cleanup\n- Add test for rate limiter maxEntries eviction behavior\n\n* fix: address audit findings across all memory-fix files\n\nclaude-sessions.ts:\n- Wrap readline loop in try/finally to ensure rl.close() on error paths\n- Guard statSync in file loop to handle files deleted between readdir and stat\n- Fix variable shadowing: rename inner `now` to `nowSec` to avoid confusion\n- Update throttle timestamp on empty scan results (prevents repeated disk scans)\n- Skip sidechain-only sessions (zero user+assistant messages)\n\nsessions.ts:\n- Decouple `active` flag from cache — compute at read time to prevent stale data\n- Remove activeWithinMs from cache key to eliminate cache thrashing between\n  callers using different windows (Infinity vs default)\n- Add invalidateSessionCache() and call it after pruneGatewaySessionsOlderThan\n\nevents/route.ts:\n- Null out cleanup after first call to prevent double-invoke\n- Remove unnecessary `if (request.signal)` guard (always defined on NextRequest)\n\nrate-limit.test.ts:\n- Rewrite eviction test with maxRequests=1 to actually prove eviction occurred\n- Add assertion that non-evicted entries remain tracked","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpt4dKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9iUQALCvxRO0W5o1Tq/LxKmLF1SK\njy6nKpEKQyqDuwEcWLn05VOBw6UIgzHuAaBULZlpZ+ADQw7W+PdCtTkTz6wQLhpw