":"https://github.com/tomwattsca","id":17442606,"login":"tomwattsca","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDQyNjA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomwattsca/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomwattsca/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomwattsca/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomwattsca/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomwattsca/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomwattsca","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/classical91/mission-control/commits/5d7b05b4f6d47416e4e08b6e2805e1e26d352e95/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-14T09:38:55Z","email":"tom@topshelfmedia.ca","name":"Tom Watts"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-14T09:38:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(tasks): use --expect-final for agent dispatch and Aegis review\n\nThe two-step agent → agent.wait pattern used in dispatchAssignedTasks and\nrunAegisReviews only returns lifecycle metadata (runId, status, timestamps).\nThe agent''s actual response text is only available via --expect-final on the\ninitial agent call, which blocks until completion and returns the full payload\nincluding result.payloads[0].text.\n\nWithout this fix:\n- Task resolution is stored as the raw wait JSON instead of the agent''s response\n- Aegis cannot parse a VERDICT from the resolution, so it always defaults to rejected\n- Tasks are permanently stuck in a reject/retry loop and never complete\n\nFix: replace the two-call pattern with a single --expect-final call in both\ndispatchAssignedTasks and runAegisReviews. Also improve sessionId extraction\nto use the agentMeta path from the final payload.\n\nCo-authored-by: Tom Watts <tom@techteamup.com>","tree":{"sha":"a20e30e86d480f21411f1e79bf35b4d29c535279","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/classical91/mission-control/git/trees/a20e30e86d480f21411f1e79bf35b4d29c535279"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/classical91/mission-control/git/commits/5d7b05b4f6d47416e4e08b6e2805e1e26d352e95","verification":{"payload":"tree a20e30e86d480f21411f1e79bf35b4d29c535279\nparent 4fa1cbd3a5bc230a8126f002cf5608c646255292\nauthor Tom Watts <tom@topshelfmedia.ca> 1773481135 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773481135 +0700\n\nfix(tasks): use --expect-final for agent dispatch and Aegis review\n\nThe two-step agent → agent.wait pattern used in dispatchAssignedTasks and\nrunAegisReviews only returns lifecycle metadata (runId, status, timestamps).\nThe agent''s actual response text is only available via --expect-final on the\ninitial agent call, which blocks until completion and returns the full payload\nincluding result.payloads[0].text.\n\nWithout this fix:\n- Task resolution is stored as the raw wait JSON instead of the agent''s response\n- Aegis cannot parse a VERDICT from the resolution, so it always defaults to rejected\n- Tasks are permanently stuck in a reject/retry loop and never complete\n\nFix: replace the two-call pattern with a single --expect-final call in both\ndispatchAssignedTasks and runAegisReviews. Also improve sessionId extraction\nto use the agentMeta path from the final payload.\n\nCo-authored-by: Tom Watts <tom@techteamup.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJptSyvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACGkQAFkcM87W2EiwVH72LLCxLMs6\nZcGqlhjhXJqwvn49HfNh0kR8CqvwbGuC0qEwB0qOXNB6zps0wo2gyv395Ni9RUVM\nFDp+OtWm6vEZSdIg2QZMJAsn8Q2dg9DS0jdWhO0kL8VENuw0yJm6qLkFagkyQpvN\nTfL/LwoqjtE7uJ5EfnRDqAmkuPv6YPNjDdzflMBK97iPJBgYjDPKjVlS/JDY3WRP\nFjxdzLHf0Gh1OwRKUoOTS/ifPIrLyAmQRatUHtDRrWHpGETWhSNCYNX8jk/6aHIS\n0euIXMM6o5hK66xhqWulRKweI4ngNgXIJxqZyRRVE0N35ytwh6qb/fWMzaWLITPL\nJvEkL8nVTmwi2MaZHuajK4D5NL4GBTVt6Ummuq1MXzVtdb4J8GKNHRLgv33v1gGh\nK3SUpk/aUZCjUehCiq65GfDfO68XmyeBhNe4651HQa8pvlPn8GlanMUZdrSaBNhn\nMn/xMfVux6eJe42RhcB2y4uI3KyjV07+WnGwJWWNacqvykrTCS17IEV7O63tAxCQ\n7s4t7+ZT0